Subject: [Krypton] Keep compiled discovery inert without explicit startup consent

The user approved only the named mDNS/service-discovery build exceptions.
The default-off Cast choice gates MediaRouterEnabled before cached/policy state,
and all net mDNS socket creation fails closed without process startup consent.
Browser startup and child process arguments propagate that consent. With Cast
off, the renderer's WebRTC mDNS feature is disabled to preserve the former
compiled-out behavior. DIAL's existing repetition patch is retained.
Adapt upstream's no-discovery registry/lister workaround to compile the
approved path while leaving its discovery inactive without startup consent.
Cast remains unpublished pending real-device/native UI and packet validation.
The backend cannot dynamically toggle media routing, so any eventual catalog
record must require restart. These guards add no polling or idle work.

